<title>BELGIUM: EU asks Spain for GSM fee clarification.</title>
<headline>EU asks Spain for GSM fee clarification.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had decided to request Spain to give it clarification on the initial licence fee imposed on Airtel Mobile for the grant of a second concession of GSM services in the country.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission considers that the initial fee distorts competition in favour of Telefonica and gives the Spanish three months to inform thr Commission on the steps it will take to secure equal conditions for GSM operations,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Airtel is a consortium owned by a group of banks including Banco Santander, and industrial and telecommunications firms including British Telecom and Airtouch Comminications</p>
